Z||000000||overlord||11-08-2000||08:37 AM||||the two dont seem to mix....we just had our first blizzard and my engine seems to get wet very easily.  (only 3 cyclinders work).<P>is there something easily i can do to help prevent from whatever is getting wet?<P>i hate having to let the car run for 10 mins after things get wet.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||11-08-2000||08:46 AM||||What's it doing when it gets wet?||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||11-08-2000||11:00 AM||||overlord,<P>Sounds like a DIS Duke that needs new plug wires.  I am so cheap, I just let mine warm up. <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||12
Z||000003||overlord||11-08-2000||06:52 PM||||when it gets wet, it only runs on 3 cylinders...eventually if its not getting wet anymore it will go back to normal..<P>It would do this in the summer when sitting while it was raining......but now that there is some snow on the roads, it will do it whenever snow swirls around..<P>My dad mentioned that its just getting wet, he had a car that used to do that.<P>btw,  1984 2.5 fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-08-2000||07:07 PM||||Buy new plug wires and if need be a new dist cap and rotor. Good plug wires will fire soaking wet on any car I've ever had.<P>If you want to keep crap out when it's parked make some grill covers out of heavy sheet rubber or plastic or even squares of plywood. Anything that won't just blow off will work.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||2xsess||11-08-2000||11:26 PM||||If it isn't a DIS engine then it sounds to me like you need a new distributor cap, also check to make sure that it seals good, I had a 86Gt that would run real crappy in the rain then I changed the Distibutor cap and all was well. <P>Good Luck<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||overlord||11-08-2000||11:30 PM||||alright,....i replaced the plug wires a year or so ago so i think they are fine.......however have no clue what the dist. cap is like......ill check there.<BR>thanx.||||reg||1
Z||000007||KevinP||11-09-2000||01:35 AM||||Same thing with my car, refused to even start anytime it was damp, so I bought new plugs, wires and replaced the cap.  Now it starts up everytime!<P>Kevin||||reg||14
Z||000008||GT Bastard||11-09-2000||08:10 AM||||Replace plugs and put some silicone around the threads.||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierospeeder||11-09-2000||08:17 PM||||I would probably change the wires, my wires usually only last a year.<P>My car would miss under load when it was really humid out, or when my wires got wet.||||reg||1
